on the northern coast of the Greek  island of Lesbos word comes that a boat  full of migrants has been spotted the  evolving crisis and grief  they've been escorted to shore by  Spanish rescuers after a failed  interception by the Turkish Coast Guard  24 people 14 Afghan is and 10 Egyptians  including a number of young children now  they are safe after being trussed to sea  by smugglers very difficult journey and  the Turks beat us a lot by hand by foot  they kick us on the ground  Europe is divided and troubled over its  attitude to migration but these people  aren't giving up on the hope of being  accepted what do you expect you expect  to live you can't live in peace in Egypt  Christians most of the people are  Muslims you must understand that Europe  cannot take in all of the people of the  world  I know I know Europe cannot take all of  the river in the world but I I feel not  peaceful in my country it has been a  journey of just six nautical miles a  route Europe was desperate to close down  if you thought the eu-turkey deal had  stopped the flow of migrants arriving  between Turkey and Greece it simply  hasn't on this one Greek island alone up  to a hundred people a day are arriving  wasn't the turkey deal supposed to stop  this it's a question I can answer but it  hasn't stopped people arriving in Greece  has it it has enough  there are an increasing number of women  and children making the perilous journey  on this route Herkimer group and with no  Greek officials in sight the welcome  here was entirely provided by  international volunteers but after so  many have come before them the reception  in the rest of Europe may not be so worn  Lisa Holland Sky News on the Greek  island of Lesbos
 

